e {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "6 –  7 August 2021"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2125"} "Makuhari Messe, 2-1, Nakase, Mihama-ku, Chiba, Chiba Prefecture, Japan"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19009648"} "16 from 16 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The #1 seed was Azerbaijani " [:a {:href "/athletes/116984"} "Mariya Stadnik"] ", who had won the 2019 World Championships and was the silver medallist in this class (then at 48 kg) at Rio and London. The second seed went to Romanian " [:a {:href "/athletes/131528"} "Emilia Vuc"] ", who had been runner-up to Stadnik at the 2019 Worlds and also had a silver medal from the 2017 Worlds. Not seeded was Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/144499"} "Yui Susaki"] ", who was World Champion in 2017 and 2018."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Both Stadnik and Susaki won their first two matches easily and met in the semi-finals, where Susaki won by technical superiority, 11-0, in 3:47, overwhelming her Azerbaijani opponent. Susaki went to the final where she faced China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/129722"} "Sun Yanan"] ", who had been World Champion back in 2013. Sun had defeated American " [:a {:href "/athletes/147309"} "Sarah Hildebrandt"] ", 2018 World silver medallist and 2019 Pan American Champion, in the semi-finals."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final was another comfortable victory for Susaki who won the gold medal by 10-0 over Sun in only 1:36. Stadnik and Hildebrandt entered the repêchage where they each won their match and shared the bronze medals. Vuc had been upset in her opening match by Bulgarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/141328"} "Miglena Selishka"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [: